{
  "id": "span-categories",
  "doc": "Which broad category a span falls in. Ordered first-match rules, like the observation type, and a **separate question with its own precedence**: a transport call is an HTTP category and a plain observation, and one dialect's operation names name an agent here where the conventions leave them unclassified there.\n\nThe transport rules come first for the same reason they do there - with a framework SDK also instrumenting, that span is a duplicate view of the real generation, and one provider's own API calls announce themselves only as an RPC system. Whether such traces are visible at all is the trace list's business.",
  "span_categories": [
    {
      "id": "category.transport",
      "rank": 10,
      "doc": "One provider's API calls arrive as `rpc.system`, and would otherwise be categorised from their `gen_ai.*` attributes as the generation they duplicate.",
      "all_of": [
        {
          "attr_exists": [
            "http.method",
            "http.request.method",
            "rpc.system"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "result": "http"
    },
    {
      "id": "category.database",
      "rank": 20,
      "all_of": [
        {
          "attr_exists": [
            "db.system"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "result": "db"
    },
    {
      "id": "category.messaging",
      "rank": 30,
      "all_of": [
        {
          "attr_exists": [
            "messaging.system"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "result": "messaging"
    },
    {
      "id": "category.object_storage",
      "rank": 40,
      "doc": "Any attribute under one provider's object-storage prefix, which is what a bucket or key operation carries.",
      "all_of": [
        {
          "attr_prefix": [
            "aws.s3."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "result": "storage"
    },
    {
      "id": "category.chat_of_an_embedding_model",
      "rank": 50,
      "doc": "The same correction the observation type makes: telemetry that reports an embedding call as a chat completion, settled by the model's own name, case-insensitively. The two model attributes are two answers to one question, so only the **first present** one is searched: a request for a chat model answered by a mislabelled response model is still a chat completion.",
      "all_of": [
        {
          "attr_equals": [
            {
              "key": "gen_ai.operation.name",
              "value": "chat"
            },
            {
              "key": "gen_ai.operation.name",
              "value": "text_completion"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text_contains": {
            "sources": [
              "attr:gen_ai.request.model",
              "attr:gen_ai.response.model"
            ],
            "needles": [
              "embed"
            ],
            "first_present_source": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "result": "embedding"
    },
    {
      "id": "category.chat",
      "rank": 60,
      "all_of": [
        {
          "attr_equals": [
            {
              "key": "gen_ai.operation.name",
              "value": "chat"
            },
            {
              "key": "gen_ai.operation.name",
              "value": "text_completion"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "result": "llm"
    },
    {
      "id": "category.embeddings",
      "rank": 70,
      "all_of": [
        {
          "attr_equals": [
            {
              "key": "gen_ai.operation.name",
              "value": "embeddings"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "result": "embedding"
    },
    {
      "id": "category.tool_execution",
      "rank": 80,
      "all_of": [
        {
          "attr_equals": [
            {
              "key": "gen_ai.operation.name",
              "value": "execute_tool"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "result": "tool"
    },
    {
      "id": "category.agent_operations",
      "rank": 90,
      "doc": "Three operation names that all mean an agent was running: the conventional one, and two a dialect adds for a group of agents and for one turn of its own loop.",
      "all_of": [
        {
          "attr_equals": [
            {
              "key": "gen_ai.operation.name",
              "value": "invoke_agent"
